(I) (नारायण)--an अवतार् of विष्णु, born of Dharma and मूर्ती, a daughter of दक्ष; आदिशेष form of Hari, distinguished for tapas;
1: भा. I. 2. 4; 3. 9; II. 7. 6-7; XII. 8. ३२, ३५. Br. II. ३५-93; M. 1. 2.
a friend and associate of नारायण said to have performed tapas at बदरी;
2: भा. III. 4. २२; IV. 1. ५२; VII. 6. २७.
seeing the sage's penance Indra got afraid and sent the God of Love and the Apsarasas to disturb his contemplation. Nara invited him and was hospitable by creating a number of beautiful women who served them; Nara asked them to choose one among them as an ornament of Heaven. So they took ऊर्वशि and narrated to Indra the superior powers of the sage;
3: Ib. XI. 4. 6-१६; 7. १८.
was seen with नारायण by मार्कण्डेय and was praised by him.
4: Ib. XII. 8. ३२, ३५, ४०-49; 9. 1.

--a दानव with मनुष्य धर्म;
1: वा. ६८. १५.
a Saimhi- keya;
2: Ib. ६८. १९.
killed by कृष्ण.
3: Ib. ९८. १०२.

--The two sages comprising the fourth अवतार् of विष्णु and born of मूर्ती; universal joy and good omens at their birth; गन्धमादन their abode;
1: भा. I. 2. 4, २६; 3. 9; IV. 1. ५२-57; Vi. V. २४. 5; ३७. ३४ and ३७.
born later as कृष्ण and अर्जुण;
2: Ib. IV. 1. ५९.
worshipped by नाभी;
3: Ib. V. 4. 4.
wor- shipped in भारतवर्ष;
4: Ib. V. १९. 9.
praised by नारद.
5: Ib. V. १९. १२-15.
To their आश्रम the sages repaired for a visit;
6: Ib. IX. 1. ३१.
shrine of, at Badar- याश्रम.
7: Ib. X. ५२. 4.

(I)--the beloved tenth son of ब्रह्मा, born of his lap; one of the twelve, who knew the धर्म ordained by Hari; a celibate; an attendant of Hari; was taught the भागवत by the father; and he gave it in his turn to व्यास; guru of विशोक (s.v.) author of सात्वततन्त्र; wor- shipped नारायण in भारतवर्ष by following the course of सान्ख्य and yoga; did not comprehend Hari's माया; faith in Kriyayoga which he expounded; in previous births, he was a Gandharva by name उपबर्हण and a son of a दासि.
1: भा. I. 4. ३२-33; II. 9. ४०-44; III. १२. २२-3; IV. 8. १५; १३. 3-4; V. १९. १०-15; VI. 3. २०; 4. ३९; VII. 1. 5; ११. 3; १५. ६९-73; X. 1. ६१ [1], ६४; ३९. ५४; ९०. ३४ [1]; XI. २७. 2; XII. 4. ४१; १३. १९; M. 3. 8; वा. 1. १३०; ६५. १३५, १४२; Br. I. 1. १११; M. 5. 5-११; वा. ६५. १३९, १४६-50, १५६.
A देवऋषि holding the वीणा in his hand; called on व्यास and complimented him on having produced the भारत and asked him why he looked uneasy; when he admitted his inability to explain the cause, the sage treated him to a dis- [page२-226+ ५०] course on devotion to Hari and incidentally gave an account of his own past; how in a previous birth he was a son of a ser- vant-maid in the service of seers and Brahmanas, how he was brought up by the latter with affection, how their asso- ciation helped him to cultivate devotion to Lord, how after their departure he wandered aimlessly with his mother who soon died, how he was sitting in the forest meditating on the Lord when He appeared in his mind; in a later Kalpa he was born of ब्रह्मा as नारद;
2: भा. I. chh. 5 and 6; वा. ५२. 3.
advised हर्यश्वास् on the path of ‘not returning’ (अनिवर्तन) which they adopted; with his mind set on ईश्वर-Brahman he advised again their brothers शबलाश्वास् in the same way and they followed it too; for so advising his sons, he was cursed by दक्ष to be always a wanderer with no settled home;
3: भा. VI. 5 (whole); Vi. V. 1. ६७; १५. 3.
accompanied Angiras to the court of Citraketu lamenting his child's death; instructed him in मन्त्रोपनिषद् to realise the presence of सन्कर्षण; showed the king and his relations the जीव of the dead child but pointing how the आत्मन् alone is eternal; the text of the विद्या imparted to Citraketu; went back to Angiras in Brahmaloka; could not find fault with Hara for violating Brahmaloka धर्म; told शुक the story of Citraketu; could not comprehend the Great Being;
4: भा. VI. १४. 9-६१; chh. १५, १६ and १७.
could not comprehend Hari's माया;
5: Ib. IX. 4. ५७.
cursed नलकूबेर and मणिग्रीव, sons of Kubera, for their intoxicated pride; his view on the merits of poverty as contrasted with wealth; went to Nara-नारायण's abode after cursing Kubera's sons;
6: Ib. X. 9. २३; १०. 8-१८, २३.
welcomed ब्रह्मा while with Priyavrata and his father Manu;
7: Ib. V. 1. 6-9, ३८.
called on प्राचीनबर्हिस् and imparted अध्यात्मतत्व by narrat- ing the story of पुरञ्जन and explaining by it the relation of जीव to परमात्म; then he went back to Siddha- loka; met प्राचेतसस् performing austerities on the western sea and advised the quick path to reach Hari; departed to Brahmaloka; sang the praise of Ananta in Brhmasabha;
8: Ib. IV. chh. २५-31; V. २५. 9.
advised हरिश्चन्द्र to pray to वरुण for a child;
9: Ib. IX. 7. 8.
spoke to ऊर्वशी of पुरूरवस् as a handsome person;
१०: Ib. IX. १४. १६.
[page२-227+ ४९] informed हिरण्याक्ष of विष्णु's residence in रसातल; spoke of Kardama's greatness and personality to देवहूती who from that time fixed her mind on him; came with and went with ब्रह्मा to see Kapila born of Kardama;
११: Ib. III. १८. 1; २२. १०-12; २४. २०.
told शिव about Sati's self-immolation in दक्ष's यज्ञ;
१२: Ib. IV. 5. 1.
met Dhruva coming out of his father's city and advised him as to the way of worshipping विष्णु by initiating him into the secret मन्त्र; met उत्तानपाद and encouraged the distressed king that the boy would soon return and add glory to his line; praised Dhruva;
१३: Ib. IV. 8. २५-69; १२. ४०-30.
learnt from Hari the true knowledge which he imparted to प्रह्लाद; saw Indra taking हिरण्यकशिपु's queen and asked him to set her at liberty which he did; then he placed her under safe custody as she was pregnant until her hus- band's return; taught to प्रह्लाद a मन्त्र sacred to Hari.
१४: Ib. IV. १९. 6.
Spoke of Jamba's death to Namuci and others. Deputed by ब्रह्मा, नारद went to Gods requesting them to no more fight the asuras;
१५: Ib. VII. 6. २७-28; 7. 7-१६.
informed Kamsa of the divinity of Vasudeva, वृष्णिस्, Nandas, and went with Gods to encourage देवकी;
१६: Ib. VIII. ११. १९-43.
induced Yavana to lay siege to मथुरा;
१७: Ib. X. 1. ६१[1]; 2. २५; Vi. V. 1. ६७.
narrated the story of Pradyumna to his parents; inform- ed मायावती that the child discovered in the fish was Pra- dyumna, काम reborn, and hence her husband; revealed Pradyumna's identity to the doubters of द्वारका;
१८: भा. X. [५०. ४४]; ५१. 5.
sang the praise of कृष्ण when he lifted the Govar- dhana; informed Kamsa that राम and कृष्ण were the sons of Vasudeva who had kept them in secret and prevented Kamsa from starting out to kill Vasudeva; told Kamsa his story of his birth; visited कृष्ण and spoke to him in secret what he was destined to do beginning with the day after when he would kill Kamsa and others and left for his place;
१९: Ib. X. ५५. 6-३६; Vi. V. २७. 9-१३, २५.
informed कृष्ण of imprisonment of Aniruddha by बाण and शाम्ब by the Kurus; visited द्वारका desirous of seeing कृष्ण in the house of each of his numerous wives at the same time and saw that ब्रह्मण्यदेव who was [page२-228+ ४९] engaged in different things at the different houses, was wel- comed separately in every house; left the place pleased; called on कृष्ण to inform him of युधिष्ठिर's desire to perform राजसूय; the purpose of his visit was accom- plished;
२०: भा. X. २७. २४; ३६. १६-19 [२७]; ३७. 9-२४; ३९. 9.
narrated in the राजसूय sacrifice of युधिष्ठिर, how Caidya the hater of Hari entered into Him, the Supreme Being, as well as the previous history of दमघोष and Dantavaktra.
२१: Ib. X. ६३. 2; ६८. १३; ६९ (whole); ७०. ३२-44; ७१. ११, १८; Vi. V. ३३. १०; ३७. 6.
Came to see भीष्म on his death-bed;
२२: भा. VII. 1. १२-43.
addressed by युधिष्ठिर, नारद said that everything was the work of time and the will of God; informed युधिष्- ठिर that धृतराष्ट्र was in the हिमालयस् engaged in the penance and would die within five days; and went back to heaven;
२३: Ib. I. 9. 6.
came to see परीक्षित् practising प्रायोपवेश;
२४: Ib. I. १३. ३७-59.
welcomed by कृष्ण, युधिष्ठिर and others, नारद, drew the attention of कृष्ण to the necessity of vanquishing शाल्व who was out to cut the root of the यादवस्; knew of कृष्ण's glory and greatness and told लक्ष्मणा of it; praised Vasudeva for his question on Karma; left for Sya- मन्तपञ्चक;
२५: Ib. I. १९. १०.
went with कृष्ण to मिथिला, heard स्रुतिगीता from नारायण at नारायणाश्रम; visited श्वेतद्वीप during Brahmasatra; called upon व्यास and communicated to him what he heard from नारायण; advised by वृत्र to worship शिव as the most easily pleased among the Gods;
२६: Ib. X. ७६. 2 [2-१०]; 3-7 [1-4]; ८३. १७; ८४. 3, ३०-33, ५७.
left with other sages for पिण्डारक; visited द्वारका and met Vasudeva; questioned by him on भागवत धर्म, he related the conversation that took place between Nimi, the Videha King, and the nine sages, the sons of ऋषभ;
२७: Ib. X. ८६. १८; ८७. 4-5, १०, ४७-8; ८८. १४-16.
views of, on thirty characteristics of धर्म, on the वर्णस् and women; on a ब्रह्मचारि, वानप्रस्थ, a Yati, and a गृहस्थ;
२८: Ib. XI. 1. १२; chh. 2-5 (whole).
enquired of ब्रह्मा the knowledge lead- ing to the realisation of आत्मन्; a महाभागवत who attained Hari through devotion.
२९: Ib. VII. chh. ११-14 (whole).
Sang a गाथ in honour of कार्तवीर्य Arjuna: compiled the नारदीय धर्म; told the रामायण to वाल्मीकि;
३०: Ib. II. 4. २५; 5. 1-8; VII. 1. ३०; XI. २७. 2.
[page२-229+ २४] learnt the details of the vow नक्षत्रपुरुष from महा- deva and of माहेश्वरव्रतम् from नन्दिकेश; on the lat- ter's advice took a bath at प्रयागा.
३१: M. ४३. २३; ४७. ३०; ५३. २३ and ७२.
Informed Maya at Tripuram of the preparations of gods to attack his city; visited इलावृतम् sacred to Bali; arranged, at the request of Indra, the marriage of उमा with शिव;
३२: Ib. ५४. 2-4; ९५. 4; १०२. १९; ११२. २१.
His sister was अरुन्दती, wife of वसिष्ठ; informed सावित्री's father of the short lease of life of the bridegroom chosen;
३३: Ib. १३४. 3-२३; १३५. 1; १५४. १११-207; १८७. १४-52; १९२. ११; २०१. ३०
cursed दक्ष's sons.
३४: Ib. २०८. १२-13.

(I)--an अवतार् with Nara; as the Supreme Being; as पुरुष and महापुरुष; Protector of the प्राणस्; is कृष्ण;
1: भा. I. 2. 4; 3. 9; II. 5. १५-16; 7. 6; १०. ११; IV. 1. ५२; V. २६. ३८; X. 6. २४; ६९. ४४; Br. II. ३५. ९३; III. 3. ६२; ३३. १६; ३५. 3, ३६-40; वा 104. ५८; १०९. २३.
identified with Veda;
2: भा. VI. 1. ४०-41.
reincarnated as अदिती's son;
3: Ib. VI. 6. ३८.
मन्त्र sacred to;
4: Ib. VI. ch. 8. (whole).
the sage of sages;
5: Ib. XI. १६. २५; XII. 8. ३२ and ४७; 9. 1.
the आश्रम of;
6: Ib. VII. १४. ३२.
born of धर्म in the चाक्षुष epoch.
7: Br. III. ७१. १९६-7; ७३. ७२.
The Lord without birth; same as विष्णु, brother of Indra; the last resort of the sages.
8: Ib. II. ३५. २०८; III. 3. १०२; M. 1. 2-3; १५४. ३५२; १६४. २७; १७२. 3-5; Vi. I. 3. 3, 8. १५; 9. ४१; २२. ८६.
The one who came out of the darkness of महा- प्रलय and created the world in its different aspects; his serpent couch on the dark waters described; approach of ब्रह्मा into नारायण's stomach, and coming out by way of the lotus;
9: Br. II. ३५. १७०; IV. ३४. ७६; M. 2. २७-37; १७८. 1.
permeates the whole universe and pervades the three worlds;
१०: वा. 1. २०४; 5. ३८; २४. 8-३५.
approached by शिव to redeem the sin of [page२-232+ ३१] brahmicide;
११: M. १८३. ८८.
the वारह अवतार् of;
१२: Br. I. 4. २७; 5. 3-5; M. २४७. 6; वा. 6. 3-७८; २१. ८१; १०३. 9.
is प्रजापति, is Brah- man;
१३: M. २४७. ३५; Br. II. 6. ६१.
is साध्य with श्री as wife;
१४: वा. ३०. ७२.
a compound of क्षेत्रज and प्रकृति for the welfare of the world;
१५: Ib. १०१. २२८.
to be remem- bered in श्राद्धस्;
१६: M. १६. ४५.
encouraged the Asuras and Devas in the churning of the ocean; praised by ब्रह्मा;
१७: Ib. १५४. ३५९; १६३. १०४; २४८. ४३; २४९. 1, 3-4, ८१; २५०. 1; २८२. 5.
represents the planet Budha; उर्वशी born of.
१८: Br. II. २४. ४९; III. 7. १६.

--the place sacred to Hari where He lives for the welfare of the world;
1: भा. VII. १४. ३२; X. ८७. 5-6.
visited by नारद (s.v.) after cursing the sons of Kubera;
2: Ib. X. १०. २३; ८७. 5-6.
the sages of कलापग्राम also lived there.
3: Ib. X. ८७. 7.
